      "id": "fb-001",
      "question": "What happens when a SIM goes offline?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 43.84,
      "answer": "When a SIM goes offline, it can lead to several challenges, such as loss of connectivity for the associated asset or tracker. This can impact data transmission, making it difficult to monitor the asset's location or status in real-time. The system aims to mitigate these issues by providing features like bundle remaining percentages and projected depletion dates for every active SIM, allowing support engineers to intervene before a unit goes offline. Additionally, the system is designed to ingest SIM data automatically from telco APIs to avoid manual updates and improve accuracy.\n\nSource: OLIWA User Stories — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
