      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 21.9,
      "answer": "IVMS (In-Vehicle Monitoring System) is a vehicle telematics solution that provides stable tracking, compliance, and report readiness. It involves creating or verifying units, ensuring correct tracker model mapping, and applying baseline alerts such as overspeed, ignition on/off, geofence in/out, and towing (if supported). Baseline reports include daily trips, stops, mileage, and driver behavior summaries if ECO/DSC is enabled.\n\nSource: NAVAS CMS User Manual — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
