    {
      "id": "fb-005",
      "question": "How do tracking tokens work?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 21.99,
      "answer": "Tracking tokens in the NAVAS ecosystem are used to pay for GPS tracking services based on time. They are billed per hour, day, or month, allowing customers to pay only when their assets are active. This model supports pause and resume functionality, which means you can stop and start tracking as needed without losing any tokens. The tokens are auto-renewed on a first-in, first-out basis, meaning the oldest tokens are used first.\n\nSource: NAVAS Token Billing Strategy — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
