      "answer": "To create a new geofence in the OLIWA mobile app, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the app and sign in.\n2. Load the map. If you see \"Map key not configured,\" contact support as the app build cannot show maps.\n3. Tap the menu icon (☰) at the top left and choose \"Geofences,\" or tap \"Geofences\" under Quick actions on the dashboard.\n4. Stay on the Zones tab and tap \"New\" at the bottom right.\n5. Choose the shape of the geofence:\n   - **Polygon**: An area with corners, requiring at least 4 points.\n   - **Line**: A route or road, requiring at least 2 points.\n   - **Circle**: A center and a radius.\n   Note: Switching the shape will clear any points you have placed.\n6. Tap the map to place the shape:\n   - For a Polygon or Line, tap each corner or point in turn. A hint at the top will count the points, e.g., \"3 points — tap Save when done.\" Use \"Undo\" to remove the last point.\n   - For a Circle, tap once to place the center, then set the size using the Radius slider, one of the presets (100 m, 500 m, 1 km, 5 km, 10 km, 50 km, 100 km), or type the radius in meters (between 50 m and 100,000 m).\n7. Tap \"Save & attach.\" This option will remain greyed out until the shape has enough points.\n8. In the \"New Geofence\" screen, enter:\n   - **Name**: At least 5 characters, e.g., \"Head Office.\"\n   - **Description**: At least 6 characters, describing what the zone is for.\n9. Tap \"Create\" to finalize the geofence.\n\nThis process will create a new geofence with the specified shape and details.",
